  "name": "healpix-resample",
  "description": "A lightweight, GPU-friendly Python package for regridding data from unstructured longitude/latitude samples onto a HEALPix grid. The PSFResampler treats projected-grid pixels as sparse, spatially weighted measurements of an unknown HEALPix field and recovers that field through a matrix-free weighted least-squares problem, jointly accounting for the sensor point spread function and the source-to-HEALPix geometry.",
